diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 84d79150ebeec58114902b2cfa9386b50497903d..6b496cde4e1319f21cd374ff33abfce1bfda8e3d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ The first implementation focuses on the web app and local Backend API. VSCode ex
 - Compare PNG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, GIF, SVG, PDF, TIFF, Excalidraw JSON, and Obsidian Excalidraw Markdown. Git treats `*.excalidraw.md` and `*_excalidraw.md` as images and decodes Obsidian's `compressed-json` drawing block.
 - Select pages independently for multi-page PDF/TIFF inputs.
 - Browse changed files in a Git working tree from a sidebar (kind icons, change badges, filter, per-file HTML export checkboxes) and compare changed image and text files, including additions, deletions, untracked files, and staged renames where the HEAD-side path differs. Markdown notes with `excalidraw-plugin: parsed` expose both a text diff and a separate embedded Excalidraw image diff; Git arrow-key navigation cycles through both targets. Dagnetz CAD Viewer blocks (```` ```step ```` / ```` ```cad ````) in a changed note appear as "3D表示 n" sub-items: the browser renders each block the way the plugin prints it (camera, section, annotations with leaders, axes) for HEAD and the working tree (blocks are matched by their `name:`, falling back to order only when one side has no name), and the two images are compared like any other image, so annotation and view changes show up alongside the 3D shape diff. STEP, STL and OBJ models are supported.
+- When the Git folder field points at a Markdown note, the "リンク先のファイルも含める" checkbox chooses whether linked images, notes, and models are listed too, or only the note itself (API: `include_links`, default `true`).
+- Open the history of any changed file with the clock-arrow button in the Git sidebar: the sidebar switches to the commits that touched the file (oldest first, following renames) plus the uncommitted working-tree change, and each step shows "parent commit → that commit" in the same image, text, 3D, or embedded-view viewer. The ↑ / ↓ keys (matching the vertical list) move between commits; past commits are read-only.
 - Show text changes in a VS Code-style side-by-side view with line numbers, strongly colored added/deleted rows, visible empty-side gaps, and inline character highlighting. For Markdown, an "ignore formatting" toggle (on by default) shows whitespace, blank-line, list-marker, numbering, emphasis-marker and horizontal-rule differences as faint "format" rows instead of changes (trailing spaces, heading levels, checkboxes, front matter and code blocks are still compared exactly). Text extensions are configurable from the hamburger menu and saved locally in the browser.
 - Add image annotations or per-file text memos from the Git tab, choose whether each changed file is included, then export the selected changes as one static, self-contained HTML report. Images, annotations, CSS, and the small content-zoom script are embedded; the report does not load external scripts, fonts, or any other network resources.
 - Align image B to image A with staged OpenCV feature matching and ECC refinement.
@@ -53,7 +55,7 @@ http://127.0.0.1:8078/
 Request/response examples for external apps are available in the app at `/api-guide` (and FastAPI's `/docs`). Detailed behavior is documented in [CLAUDE.md](claude.md).
 
 - File diff: `GET /api/health`, `POST /api/attachments`, `POST /api/analyze`, `POST /api/convert`, `POST /api/diff`, `POST /api/rediff`, `GET /api/diff/{result_id}`
-- Git diff: `POST /api/git/images`, `POST /api/git/files`, `POST /api/git/markdown` / `GET /api/git/markdown?path=...`, `GET /api/git/path?path=...`, `POST /api/git/item`, `POST /api/git/text-diff`, `POST /api/git/save-text`, `POST /api/git/revert-line`, `POST /api/git/commit`, `POST /api/git/diff`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/jobs`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/model`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/diff`
+- Git diff: `POST /api/git/images`, `POST /api/git/files`, `POST /api/git/markdown` / `GET /api/git/markdown?path=...`, `GET /api/git/path?path=...`, `POST /api/git/item`, `POST /api/git/history`, `POST /api/git/text-diff`, `POST /api/git/save-text`, `POST /api/git/revert-line`, `POST /api/git/commit`, `POST /api/git/diff`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/jobs`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/model`, `POST /api/git/cad-view/diff`
 - 3D diff: `GET /api/3d/status`, `GET /api/3d/samples`, `POST /api/3d/samples/load`, `POST /api/3d/jobs`, `GET /api/3d/jobs/{job_id}`, `GET /api/3d/jobs/{job_id}/mesh/{side}`, `DELETE /api/3d/jobs/{job_id}`, `POST /api/git/3d/jobs`
 - Settings and reports: `GET /api/settings/obsidian`, `PUT /api/settings/obsidian`, `POST /api/reports/save`
 - Ecosystem (for the opencode harness and the other apps): `GET /api/ecosystem` (app manifest: version, deep links, operations), `POST /api/ecosystem/diff` (compare two local files by path; returns numbers and 3x3 positions only, no images; does not open the browser unless `open_browser` is true)
